"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1721-6540"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology, Care Sciences and Society, Division of Family Medicine and Primary Care, Karolinska Institute, Stockholm, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"Academic Primary Care Centre, Stockholm, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Giezeman M","lastName":"Giezeman","firstName":"Maaike","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6261-6925"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Medical Sciences, Faculty of Medicine and Health, Örebro University, Örebro, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"Centre for Clinical Research and Education, Karlstad, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Janson C","lastName":"Janson","firstName":"Christer","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medical Sciences, Respiratory, Allergy and Sleep Research, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Kisiel MA","lastName":"Kisiel","firstName":"Marta A","initials":"MA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medical Sciences, Occupational and Environmental Medicine, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Eliason G","lastName":"Eliason","firstName":"Gabriella","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Respiratory Medicine, Faculty of Medicine and Health, Örebro University, Örebro, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Nager A","lastName":"Nager","firstName":"Anna","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology, Care Sciences and Society, Division of Family Medicine and Primary Care, Karolinska Institute, Stockholm, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Montgomery S","lastName":"Montgomery","firstName":"Scott","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Clinical Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Medical Sciences, Faculty of Medicine and Health, Örebro University, Örebro, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"Clinical Epidemiology Division, Department of Medicine, Karolinska Institute, Stockholm, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"Department of Epidemiology and Public Health, University College, London, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Sundh J","lastName":"Sundh","firstName":"Josefin","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Respiratory Medicine, Faculty of Medicine and Health, Örebro University, Örebro, Sweden."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6261-6925"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1721-6540"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"45","journalIssueId":4285376,"dateOfPublication":"2027 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2027,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Scand J Prim Health Care","title":"Scandinavian journal of primary health care","essn":"1502-7724","issn":"0281-3432","nlmid":"8510679","isoabbreviation":"Scand J Prim Health Care"},"printPublicationDate":"2027-12-01"},"pubYear":"2027","pageInfo":"2747915","abstractText":"<h4>Purpose</h4>Clinical features of COPD and asthma overlap, complicating differential diagnosis. This study investigated the prevalence of comorbid asthma in COPD patients and its association with patient-related outcomes.<h4>Materials and methods</h4>Patients with a doctor's diagnosis of COPD were randomly selected in two cohorts 2005 (<i>n</i> = 1060) and 2014 (<i>n</i> = 1671), from primary and secondary care in Sweden. Data were collected from medical records and patient questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up (2012 and 2022, respectively). Questionnaires included data on exacerbations. Symptoms were assessed using the clinical COPD questionnaire (CCQ). Comorbid asthma was identified through medical records. Ten-year mortality data were obtained from national registers. Logistic and linear regression assessed associations with patient-reported outcomes; Cox regression was applied for mortality analyses.<h4>Results</h4>Comorbid asthma was found in 22% of the 2005 cohort and 9% of the 2014 cohort (<i>p</i> < .001). In both cohorts, it was associated with an increased risk of exacerbations: OR (95% CI) 1.58 (1.07-2.32), <i>p</i> = .02, and 2.20 (1.38-3.52), <i>p</i> < .001, respectively. No associations were found between comorbid asthma and worsening of health status (CCQ). Mortality risk did not differ in the 2005 cohort, HR (95% CI) 0.92 (0.71-1.18), but was lower in the 2014 cohort, HR (95% CI) 0.67 (0.49-0.93), <i>p</i> = .02.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Comorbid asthma in COPD has changed from 22 to 9%, potentially due to improved diagnostics. Comorbid asthma remains clinically relevant due to its association with an increased exacerbation risk.","affiliation":"School of Medical Sciences, Faculty of Medicine and Health, Örebro University, Örebro, Sweden.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Asthma","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Pulmonary Disease, Chronic Obstructive","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CO","qualifierName":"complications"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MO","qualifierName":"mortality"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Disease Progression"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Prevalence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cohort Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Comorbidity"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Middle Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descripto