","firstName":"Patrick","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Respiratory Medicine Department, University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Arshad SH","lastName":"Arshad","firstName":"Syed Hasan","initials":"SH","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Clinical and Experimental Sciences, Faculty of Medicine, University of Southampton, UK; National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) Southampton Biomedical Research Centre at University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK; The David Hide Asthma & Allergy Research Centre, St Mary's Hospital, Newport, Isle of Wight, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Djukanovic R","lastName":"Djukanovic","firstName":"Ratko","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Clinical and Experimental Sciences, Faculty of Medicine, University of Southampton, UK; National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) Southampton Biomedical Research Centre at University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Dabrio-Reina E","lastName":"Dabrio-Reina","firstName":"Elena","initials":"E","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) Southampton Biomedical Research Centre at University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Vladimirovna Vorobeva E","lastName":"Vladimirovna Vorobeva","firstName":"Elena","initials":"E","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Clinical and Experimental Sciences, Faculty of Medicine, University of Southampton, UK; National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) Southampton Biomedical Research Centre at University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Kurukulaaratchy R","lastName":"Kurukulaaratchy","firstName":"Ramesh","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Clinical and Experimental Sciences, Faculty of Medicine, University of Southampton, UK; National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) Southampton Biomedical Research Centre at University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK; Respiratory Medicine Department, University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust, Southampton, UK; The David Hide Asthma & Allergy Research Centre, St Mary's Hospital, Newport, Isle of Wight, UK. Electronic address: Rjk1s07@soton.ac.uk."}]}}]},"journalInfo":{"journalIssueId":4276179,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Allergy Clin Immunol Pract","title":"The journal of allergy and clinical immunology. In practice","essn":"2213-2201","issn":"2213-2198","nlmid":"101597220","isoabbreviation":"J Allergy Clin Immunol Pract"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-10-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"S2213-2198(26)00907-4","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Sex disparity has been demonstrated within difficult-to-treat (difficult) asthma, with females reported to have greater disease severity and more comorbidities. Deeper understanding of these differences could help personalise management approaches.<h4>Objective</h4>To assess differences in disease characteristics between males and females with difficult asthma.<h4>Methods</h4>The Wessex AsThma CoHort study collected data from 500 patients across Southern England. Patient demographics, asthma and its treatment history, allergies, comorbidities, radiology, biological samples, lung function, and questionnaire data were subjected to univariable analyses to identify sex differences. Variables were then further assessed in multivariable regression models.<h4>Results</h4>Males were older at disease onset and were more often ex-smokers. In multivariable regression models they had higher serum immunoglobulin E (ratio 1.95, 95% CI 1.19 to 3.20) and plasma inflammatory cytokine expression (interleukin-17, tumour necrosis factor - alpha, C-C motif ligands 3 and 11 and chitinase 3-like 1). Males had poorer lung function (forced expiratory volume in 1 second effect -9.98, 95% CI -15.21 to -4.74) and more frequently had nasal polyps. Females had higher Body Mass Index, and in multivariable regression higher plasma adipokine (ratio 1.25, 95% CI 1.12 to 1.37) and interleukin-5 expression (effect 3.52, 95% CI 2.65 to 4.39), multimorbidity burden (score effect 0.60, 95% CI 0.29 to 0.92), anxiety/depression, and inducible laryngeal obstruction (odds ratio 2.38, 95% CI 1.20 to 4.76). They self-reported worse Hull Cough Hypersensitivity, Nijmegen and Sino-Nasal Outcome Test scores. We observed no difference in treatment and healthcare utilisation, or composite asthma severity score.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Sex influences difficult asthma phenotype but contrasting factors are associated with similar overall disease severity in both sexes. Males have worse lung function and systemic inflammatory profiles, whilst females experience greater psychophysiological comorbidity and multimorbidity burden. Recognising differences and considering them clinically to fine-tune management may help improve difficult asthma outcomes.","affiliation":"School of Clinical and Experimental Sciences, Faculty of Medicine, University of Southampton, UK.","publicationStatus":"aheadofprint","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Sex","Phenotype","Comorbidities","Difficult-to-treat Asthma"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaip.2026.10.028"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-30","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-30","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-10-30","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-30","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-31","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42922053","source":"MED","pmid":"42922053","doi":"10.1111/pai.70520","title":"Daycare attendance, breastfeeding, and risk of asthma in the prospective MoBa and DIPP birth cohorts.","authorString":"Tall S, Rantala AK, Takkinen HM, Korhonen TE, Kaila M, Størdal K, Tapia G, Hyöty H, Veijola R, Toppari J, Knip M, Stene LC, Virtanen SM.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Tall S","lastName":"Tall","firstName":"Susanna","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3746-4728"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Program for Clinical and Molecular Metabolism, Faculty of Medicine, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Public Health, Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare, Helsinki, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Rantala AK","lastName":"Rantala","firstName":"Aino K","initials":"AK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4845-076X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chronic Diseases, Norwegian Institute of Public Health, Oslo, Norway."},{"affiliation":"Center for Environmental and Respiratory Health Research (CERH), Research Unit of Population Health, University of Oulu, Oulu, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Takkinen HM","lastName":"Takkinen","firstName":"Hanna-Mari","initials":"HM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Public Health, Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare, Helsinki, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Unit of Health Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Tampere University, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Wellbeing Services County of Pirkanmaa, Tampere University Hospital, Tampere, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Korhonen TE","lastName":"Korhonen","firstName":"Tuuli E","initials":"TE","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Public Health, Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare, Helsinki, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Kaila M","lastName":"Kaila","firstName":"Minna","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9645-4925"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Public Health Medicine, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatrics, Tampere University Hospital, Tampere, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Størdal K","lastName":"Størdal","firstName":"Ketil","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7826-8646"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatric Research, Institute of Clinical Medicine, Faculty of Medicine, University of Oslo, Oslo, Norway."},{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatric and Adolescent Medicine, Oslo University Hospital, Oslo, Norway."}]}},{"fullName":"Tapia G","lastName":"Tapia","firstName":"German","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1770-1183"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chronic Diseases, Norwegian Institute of Public Health, Oslo, Norway."}]}},{"fullName":"Hyöty H","lastName":"Hyöty","firstName":"Heikki","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatrics, Tampere University Hospital, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Virology, Faculty of Medicine and Health Technology, Tampere University, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Fimlab Laboratories, Tampere, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Veijola R","lastName":"Veijola","firstName":"Riitta","initials":"R","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6557-270X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Research Unit of Clinical Medicine, Medical Research Center, University of Oulu, Oulu, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Children and Adolescents, Medical Research Center, Oulu University Hospital, Oulu, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Toppari J","lastName":"Toppari","firstName":"Jorma","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2228-334X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Centre for Integrative Physiology and Pharmacology, Institute of Biomedicine, University of Turku, Turku, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Centre for Population Health Research, University of Turku, and Turku University Hospital, Turku, Finland."},{"affiliation":"InFLAMES Research Flagship Center, University of Turku, Turku, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Turku University Hospital, Turku, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Knip M","lastName":"Knip","firstName":"Mikael","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0474-0033"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Program for Clinical and Molecular Metabolism, Faculty of Medicine, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatrics, Tampere University Hospital, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Pediatric Research Center, New Children's Hospital, Helsinki University Hospital, Helsinki, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Stene LC","lastName":"Stene","firstName":"Lars C","initials":"LC","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8434-119X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chronic Diseases, Norwegian Institute of Public Health, Oslo, Norway."}]}},{"fullName":"Virtanen SM","lastName":"Virtanen","firstName":"Suvi M","initials":"SM","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8928-0878"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Unit of Health Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Tampere University, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Wellbeing Services County of Pirkanmaa, Tampere University Hospital, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatrics, Tampere University Hospital, Tampere, Finland."},{"affiliation":"Centre for Child, Adolescent and Maternal Health Research (TamCAM), Tampere University, Tampere, Finland."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7826-8646"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8928-0878"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1770-1183"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3746-4728"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4845-076X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6557-270X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8434-119X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9645-4925"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0474-0033"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2228-334X"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"10","volume":"37","journalIssueId":4276755,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Pediatr Allergy Immunol","title":"Pediatric allergy and immunology : official publication of the European Society of Pediatric Allergy and Immunology","essn":"1399-3038","issn":"0905-6157","nlmid":"9106718","isoabbreviation":"Pediatr Allergy Immunol"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-10-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e70520","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Daycare attendance and breastfeeding have been associated with asthma risk. However, it remains unclear whether the association between breastfeeding and asthma risk depends on daycare attendance. We investigated whether daycare attendance acts as a modifier in the relationship between breastfeeding and asthma risk.<h4>Methods</h4>We included 72,558 children from the MoBa and 3015 children from the DIPP studies. Current asthma at age 7 years in MoBa and time to asthma by the age 5 years in DIPP were analyzed.<h4>Results</h4>In both cohorts, approximately 4% of participants were diagnosed with asthma. In MoBa, breastfeeding was associated with lower risk of overall asthma (adjusted risk ratio, aRR 0.99 [95% CI, 0.98-1.00]) and nonatopic asthma (aRR 0.97 [95% CI, 0.96-0.99]) in children who had attended daycare by the age of 18 months, and it was associated with higher overall asthma (aRR 1.01 [95% CI, 1.00-1.02]) and atopic asthma risk (aRR 1.03 [95% CI, 1.01-1.06]) in children who had not attended daycare by that age (all interaction p values ≤.05). In DIPP, the duration of breastfeeding was inversely associated with risk of atopic asthma only in an exploratory analysis in those who had started daycare by the age of 12 months (adjusted hazard ratio, aHR 0.75 [95% CI, 0.59-0.95]) but not in children who had started daycare at the age of 13-24 months (adjusted hazard ratio, aHR 1.03 [95% CI, 0.96-1.10]) or had not started daycare by the age of 24 months (adjusted hazard ratio, aHR 1.00 [95% CI, 0.94-1.06]) (interaction p value .04).<h4>Conclusions</h4>While the primary analysis in the MoBa study suggested that age at daycare entry might mildly modify the association of breastfeeding with asthma risk, in the DIPP study an interaction only appeared in an exploratory analysis with limited atopic asthma cases. Consequently, these findings represent inconsistent evidence.","affiliation":"Research Program for Clinical and Molecular Metabolism, Faculty of Medicine, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Asthma","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Risk Factors"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Prospective Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":